  "reading": "The prime-free-of-pole part of the target is a Z operator whose least eigenvalue is a Perron-root deficit, so a single positive trial function brackets it from both sides. Its one negative direction is essentially cosh(x/2), which is the positive direction of the pole form, and Weil positivity forces the elementary necessary condition alpha_L <= 2 sinh(L/2) + L. That condition is sharp: the relative margin falls from 9e-2 at L = 1/2 to 2e-3 at L = 4 while both sides grow like e^{L/2}.",
